NVFP4 routed experts for qwen3_5_moe ModelOpt checkpoints on CUDA (TensorFold 1.1.7).

Stock 1.1.7 reads Qwen3.5-MoE (Ornith-1.5-122B) only as MLX affine or EXL3: cuda_geometry.zig refused a ModelOpt
config for the MoE type ("the routed experts read MLX tables only"), although the dense 27B already serves ModelOpt
NVFP4/FP8 and the core has NVFP4 grouped experts (cuda.experts.Nvfp4Experts, GLM's and Flash Next's). This patch:
  - cuda_geometry.zig: admits a qwen3_5_moe config whose quantization_config is quant_method "modelopt" (other
    formats' experts stay refused, as before);
  - cuda_modelopt.zig: a MoE layer's kinds skip the dense MLP slots and require its routed experts ("mlp.experts")
    and shared expert to be NVFP4 (NVFP4 or W4A16_NVFP4); compressed-tensors MoE exports stay refused;
  - cuda_modelopt_experts.zig (new): each layer's 256 routed experts and the shared one (last), read as stored
    (e2m1 codes, e4m3 block scales, the fp32 weight_scale_2 per projection, gate and up apart) and packed on the host
    by Nvfp4Experts.packGateUp/packOne (32 experts at a time over the CPU's cores) straight into the arena; the
    router rows (mlp.gate, then shared_expert_gate) as stored bf16;
  - cuda_weights.zig, cuda_engine.zig, cuda_routed.zig: the arena counts them, the engine loads the NVFP4 expert
    kernels for such a checkpoint, and the routed rows dispatch format .nvfp4 (bf16 rows in, W4A16 arithmetic).
Attention/GDN projections (FP8, per-tensor scale), in_proj_a/b (bf16) and lm_head (W4A16 NVFP4) already load through
the dense family's ModelOpt path, with bf16 activations against the stored weights.
Verified on a GB10 with ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-122B-NVFP4: loads in ~50 s (model 70.26 GiB); teacher-forced NLL on
15,853 tokens of four texts 1.2804 vs SGLang's 1.2848 on the same checkpoint and ids (bench/nll.py, README);
host tests test-qwen35-modelopt-admission-host and test-qwen35-formats-host pass.

